<title>USA: Duke Realty sells $50 mln in notes.</title>
<headline>Duke Realty sells $50 mln in notes.</headline>
<dateline>INDIANAPOLIS 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duke Realty Investments Inc said Thursday it issued $50 million in medium-term notes from an existing shelf registration.</p>
<p>The proceeds of the notes will be used to pay down Duke's line of credit and to fund acquisition and development of commercial properties, the company said.</p>
<p>The notes have an eight-year term and are due in November 2004, the company said. The fixed interest rate on the notes is 7.14 percent which represents a spread of 80 basis points over the applicable U.S. Treasury security.</p>
<p>	    -- Reuter Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
